            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "OMG! My husband and I LOVE wings and we make our own hot sauce so we rarely venture to make any \"different\" kinds of sauces. Well, this little gem is a real winner and I'm so glad I tried it - no changes at all. It's fabulous! It's a little heat with a little sweet! If you love wings you have to try this recipe at least once......"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy Heironimus Castle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this with chicken breasts and it turned out great. I used dried cilantro instead of basil, and only used 3 cloves of garlic. I put the extra marinade on the stove and simmered it for 10 minutes and poured it over the chicken and rice. Really good!",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-26T06:26:24.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristy Guillotte"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the best chicken wing sauce ever! I had 9 large chicken drumsticks, first I took 1 cup flour, 1/2 cup bread crumbs, salt and pepper, mixed in a bowl,I coated the chicken in this mixture. then I melted 1/2 stick of butter and poured it into a disposable foil lasagna pan coating the bottom of the pan, place the chicken in the pan and bake 20 minutes at 400 degrees turn chicken and bake 20 more minutes. when chicken is done coat with saauce and enjoy! can't wait to use this on bonless chicken strips. Thanks for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-09T04:49:04.137Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JLANAM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used Honey Mustard Dressing II from this site, which we LOVE, but it's more of a dressing/dip. I'd say to make sure your honey mustard doesn't have a mayo base, and I think I'd try it with less butter. It tasted a little too mayonnaise-y and greasy the first day, but it was great the next day. It reminds us of the Colorado Coppers wings at our favorite wing place ever!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-08T14:18:17.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Singer6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were OK. Maybe it was the honey mustard I used (French's) but the mustard really was overpowering. If I made these again I would try a different brand of honey mustard and do a 1/2 1/2 ratio for hot pepper sauce and honey mustard.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-28T07:59:06.833Z"
          },
          {
